1
00:00:00,599 --> 00:00:02,799
(Amy:)Oh, well, you know,

2
00:00:02,801 --> 00:00:05,231
now-now that I'm hearing it,
it does sound familiar.

3
00:00:05,237 --> 00:00:06,437
(Sheldon:)How could it?

4
00:00:06,438 --> 00:00:08,768
(Sheldon:)I never told you,
and you never bothered to ask.

5
00:00:08,774 --> 00:00:10,804
(Amy:)Well, now I know.
Yeah.

6
00:00:13,012 --> 00:00:15,442
(Meemaw:)So, Penny, I understand
you have a new job.

7
00:00:15,447 --> 00:00:16,517
(Penny:)Yes.

8
00:00:16,515 --> 00:00:17,785
(Penny:)I'm a pharmaceutical
sales rep.

9
00:00:17,783 --> 00:00:19,113
(Sheldon:)Oh.

10
00:00:19,118 --> 00:00:22,658
(Meemaw:)It's so wonderful that
you modern gals can have it all.

11
00:00:23,555 --> 00:00:25,925
(Meemaw:)A husband
and a full-time career.

12
00:00:25,924 --> 00:00:29,094
(Amy:)I have a relationship
and a full-time career, too.

13
00:00:29,094 --> 00:00:31,794
(Meemaw:)That doesn't bode well.

14
00:00:34,433 --> 00:00:37,533
Why not? You-you just said
it's okay for her to work.

15
00:00:37,536 --> 00:00:41,336
(Meemaw:)Well, Leonard doesn't need as
much tending to as Sheldon does.

16
00:00:41,340 --> 00:00:42,440
(Meemaw:)And as Moon Pie explained,

17
00:00:42,441 --> 00:00:45,041
(Meemaw:)Leonard's work

18
00:00:45,044 --> 00:00:47,414
(Meemaw:)is more of a hobby.

19
00:00:48,881 --> 00:00:50,781
(Leonard:)That's my best friend.

20
00:00:50,783 --> 00:00:52,013
(Penny:)Yeah.

21
00:00:52,017 --> 00:00:53,417
AMY:
Look,

22
00:00:53,419 --> 00:00:55,349
I-I get that you're protective
of your grandson,

23
00:00:55,354 --> 00:00:57,384
(Amy:)but he's an adult now.

24
00:00:57,389 --> 00:01:01,029
(Amy:)Maybe I understand what he needs
better than you do.

